{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885804-ways-to-disguise-a-ghouls-relationship-with-you-if-your-not-rich","id":885804,"title":"Ways to disguise a ghouls relationship with you if your not rich.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-08T17:12:46-07:00","id":885804,"title":"Ways to disguise a ghouls relationship with you if your not rich.","content":"If a Kindreds Rich, its to be expected, he'd have a Maid or butler.<br /> <br /> but otherwise...<br /> <br /> Remember an abridged version of three musketeers Read in grade school<br /> <br /> D'artegnan was being told to hire a man, because he needed a personal servant<br /> <br /> He said &quot;He looks like a fool&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You have no money, you need a servant, a fools what you WANT&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> how to explain him having a servant on 24/7 Call.<br /> <br /> Some possibletys.<br /> <br /> &quot;Were friends, we just hang out a lot.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Were Dating/Married.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Were related (may or may not be true)<br /> <br /> <br /> any other ideas for how to explain you having a Servant in spite of not appearently being able to afford one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T17:33:44-07:00","id":885823,"title":"","content":"Ghouls need to sleep as well, characters need privacy, and some assignments are better carried off by a lone agent; why are you assuming that once you ghoul a person they become an inseparable &quot;party member&quot;?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't see anyone going around some restaurant's patron tables inquiring about the nature of their relationship, for example.<br /> <br /> Let people bias color their opinions. You don't need to yell &quot;WE'RE ON A DATE!&quot; to justify your presence there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:13:41-07:00","id":885878,"title":"","content":"Is this a question or just a thread for ideas? <br /> <br /> You don't need to be rich to have friends, family, lovers, maid/butler. A ghoul can be pretty much anything you can think of. I agree with Ephsy you don't really need to make a strange announcement. <br /> <br /> And they don't need to be there 24/7","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:23:26-07:00","id":885884,"title":"","content":"Anything that helps explain (or make it look like you're the treatment, not the cause) occasional illness and/or whatever weird behaviors tend to crop up in ghouls, given feeding Conditions, how unhealthy their relationships often are, and the adjustments of becoming a minor template. Doctor, psychiatrist, priest, AA sponsor, rehab, or therapist fit the bill, and as a bonus most of 'em are authority figures.<br /> <br /> Remember that Ghouls are bound and probably addicted, so you can more or less dictate how much or little contact you have with them (within reason). Masseuse, tutor, home charity, handyman, on-call vet, any kind of trainer or instructor on a budget makes a good cover, for either party. Any activity requiring a modicum of privacy and casual interaction, that can be stepped up, wound down, or abandoned, without suspicion.<br /> <br /> Of course, an easier solution is just to ghoul an antisocial someone and use <i>their </i>money and home. Just make sure you save up Experiences to buy the Merit before your ST starts messing with your freely-acquired stuff.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T04:58:08-07:00","id":886110,"title":"","content":"Had been thinking of that, its a good way to get a cheap haven... sure that in a lot of those cases where their new childe is wealthy, or was a title holding noble,, their sire would move in with them, rather then vise versa","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:23:06-07:00","id":886157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885804-ways-to-disguise-a-ghouls-relationship-with-you-if-your-not-rich#post885804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Kindreds Rich, its to be expected, he'd have a Maid or butler.<br /> <br /> but otherwise...<br /> <br /> Remember an abridged version of three musketeers Read in grade school<br /> <br /> D'artegnan was being told to hire a man, because he needed a personal servant<br /> <br /> He said &quot;He looks like a fool&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You have no money, you need a servant, a fools what you WANT&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> how to explain him having a servant on 24/7 Call.<br /> <br /> Some possibletys.<br /> <br /> &quot;Were friends, we just hang out a lot.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Were Dating/Married.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Were related (may or may not be true)<br /> <br /> <br /> any other ideas for how to explain you having a Servant in spite of not appearently being able to afford one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>red hood the gangrel had her ghoul pose as her parent.<br /> Ghouls don't have stay with you. some of the most useful ones don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:36:22-07:00","id":886681,"title":"","content":"like if you ghoul someone on the police force to try subverting it.<br /> <br /> Curious do you want someone who goes on patrol, who'll hopefully find something that needs buried.<br /> <br /> or someone who works at the station... though what to instruct him to do if he hears of something needing buried then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:04:33-07:00","id":886853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885804-ways-to-disguise-a-ghouls-relationship-with-you-if-your-not-rich?p=885823#post885823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls need to sleep as well, characters need privacy, and some assignments are better carried off by a lone agent; why are you assuming that once you ghoul a person they become an inseparable &quot;party member&quot;?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't see anyone going around some restaurant's patron tables inquiring about the nature of their relationship, for example.<br /> <br /> Let people bias color their opinions. You don't need to yell &quot;WE'RE ON A DATE!&quot; to justify your presence there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True, and unless bystanders are also following you around 24/7, then it's highly unlikely they would even notice the Ghoul as a constant presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:41:02-07:00","id":886889,"title":"","content":"You should be okay as long as you keep them from going all Renfield. If you're going to have them take Breaking Points for you, make sure it's someone who can handle it. Though there's always a chance that you can be their next Breaking Point so perhaps don't.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't even up all the day, so their ghouls certainly wouldn't be with them that whole time, unless they were a particularly servile one. The vampire is in the position of power, and can arrange when the meetings occur for the most part.<br /> <br /> As for police, it really depends on your goal. 'Subverting' an entire police force would probably be best done by controlling people high up in the ranks, commissioners and majors and councilmen. Look at something like Hamsterdam, it's not something you could pull off without someone high up allowing it. If you just have patrol cops under control, if numbers get bad in one area, someone's going to go above their heads and your ghouls are going to find themselves under suspicion.<br /> <br /> But if you just want someone to be a cop who does stuff for you like roust people out of certain areas a regular officer could do it. A detective would have more rank and probably be able to look further into certain crimes. Someone working in admin could just keep you informed of activities. I forget which of the clanbooks, I want to say Nosferatu, has a vampire called the Dead Lieutenant, who still works for the police and obviously has a lot of sway with them. If you want more specific information about what positions do what, you could check out Tales from the 13th Precinct. It's pretty heavy reading but does go into a lot of depth about the local law enforcement system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}